# Phase 18 compatibility release gate — 2026-10-22 03:16:13 UTC

Base revision: `958a047a`. This entry records the request 321
`queryConsumeQueue` protocol and RPC slice. Pinned Java source is
`efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9`.

## Compatibility changes

- Added `QueryConsumeQueueRequestHeader` with nullable topic/group and inherited
  RPC fields, primitive zero defaults, Java-tolerant malformed-number decode,
  and inherited RPC equality semantics.
- Added `QueryConsumeQueueResponseBody` and `ConsumeQueueData`, preserving
  Java property names/defaults, nullable fields and rows, nested
  `SubscriptionData`, and mutable aliases.
- Added `MQClientApi::query_consume_queue` for request 321, configured VIP
  transformation, the caller timeout, nullable response bodies, and Broker
  error mapping.
- Added invoked Java/Rust cases for populated/default/null/missing/malformed
  bodies, null request strings, Broker rejection, timeout, and VIP routing.
  Added header decode-mode checks, API inventory assertions, and bidirectional
  typed-header/body cross-decodes.
- Updated the direct reverse-audit list from 10 to 9 open operations. The wider
  P18-V01 audit and other Phase 18 work remain open.

